# Architecture

This is a CLI proxy configuration checker (VLESS, Trojan, VMess, Shadowsocks). Python orchestrates Xray subprocesses; it does not implement proxy protocols.

## Module layout

```
src/
├── __main__.py       # `python -m src` entry
├── main.py           # thin CLI (run / test commands)
├── constants/        # env-backed settings
├── services/         # business logic
│   ├── pipeline.py   # orchestration
│   ├── gateway.py    # Russian gateway session
│   ├── fetcher.py    # subscription fetching
│   ├── checker.py    # health check (port, IP, GeoIP)
│   ├── runner.py     # concurrent test runner
│   └── telegram.py   # publish configs that work in Russia
├── resources/        # file I/O
│   ├── configs.py
│   ├── results.py
│   ├── subscriptions.py
│   └── dedupe.py
└── utils/            # low-level helpers
    ├── proxy/        # proxy URL parsing and Xray config assembly
    │   ├── config.py
    │   ├── vless.py
    │   ├── trojan.py
    │   ├── vmess.py
    │   └── shadowsocks.py
    ├── xray.py       # Xray subprocess lifecycle
    └── subscription.py
```

## Rules

- Keep orchestration in `main.py` and `services/pipeline.py` thin — delegate to services.
- Xray process management stays in `utils/xray.py`.
- Protocol parsing and per-protocol Xray outbounds stay in `utils/proxy/`; dispatch via `utils/proxy/__init__.py`.
- Health checks stay in `services/checker.py`.
- File I/O stays in `resources/`.
- Use `asyncio.Semaphore` for concurrency — no custom worker pool.
